# Fixture: Europe base with the nation's boycott_bitmap = Tobacco (bit 2) and only 1500 gold; a Galleon in the harbor holds
# Tobacco 100 / Cotton 40 / Tobacco 60. Back taxes = ask (5 bid + 1 burden = 6) x 500 = 3000 > 1500.
# Clicking the boycotted market cell raises @KISSUP (two rows: refuse, then "Pay 3000"); the purse is only tested after Pay.
# Hold i is at x = 152+12i, y 171; market cell i at x = 10+19i, y 189; @KISSUP rows at y 156 (refuse) and 168 (Pay).
key e                    # open the European Status screen
wait 10
click 48 189             # Tobacco cell: @KISSUP quoting 3000
click 150 168            # "Pay 3000.": gold 1500 < 3000 -> @KISSSORRY "we only have 1500 available", nothing changes
key Return               # OK the @KISSSORRY popup
click 48 189             # @KISSUP again
click 150 156            # first row (decline): nothing changes
drag 152 171 48 189      # Tobacco still refused: @KISSUP again, trade aborted whatever the answer
key Return               # decline @KISSUP (row 0 = refuse)
key l                    # buy on the selected boycotted Tobacco cell: @KISSUP instead of the @HOWMUCH4 prompt
key Return               # decline as well
drag 164 171 67 189      # Cotton (not boycotted) sells: 40 @ 4 = 160, tax 9, net 151
key e                    # leave Europe
